{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"thoughtful-amoebaean-mongrel","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nsrc/rebar/_commands/compact.py is 793 LOC (7 under the 800 hard cap) and hosts three active complexity-baseline entries: _compact_locked (CCN 24), rebuild_snapshot_from_full_log (21), compact_all_cli (17). Splitting it along seams naturally lowers both size and local complexity. ZERO in-progress contention.\n\n## Plan\n- Extract a cohesive cluster (e.g. the snapshot-rebuild path) into a sibling module along an existing call-graph seam.\n- Where the extraction naturally simplifies _compact_locked / rebuild_snapshot_from_full_log, reduce their branching; do not force complexity below the ratchet artificially.\n- Update the shrink-only complexity baseline (.github/complexity-baseline.json) only downward.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] src/rebar/_commands/compact.py at/below the 500-LOC target; new sibling >=100 LOC on a real seam.\n- [ ] Complexity baseline entries for compact.py are equal or lower (shrink-only ratchet respected).\n- [ ] Behavior preserved; module-size, complexity, type, lint, and test gates green.\n\n## Non-overlap\nTouches src/rebar/_commands/compact.py, a new sibling under src/rebar/_commands/, and the shrink-only .github/complexity-baseline.json entries for this file — free of in-progress contention.","id":"b2bb-fa81-e054-4fb5","parent_id":"2fe0-ce8b-4715-4e07","priority":3,"tags":["remediation","file-size","complexity","ae1b"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Split near-cap module _commands/compact.py (793 LOC) and reduce its local complexity"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786219932935055001,"uuid":"d30e74ca-84c9-48b3-9017-058e159c